# T4.2 case 3a: the database is stopped while the tab is connected, and the
# reconnect that follows has to fail rather than hang.
#
# The runner waits for `connected.txt`, stops the container, and has the whole
# `wait` below to finish doing it — ten seconds, against a `docker stop -t 5`
# that is done in six. It starts the container again as soon as this script is
# done, so the server is away for the rest of this wait and no longer.
key c
wait busy
expect ●
expect connected in
frame connected

wait 10000
key c
wait busy
expect ✗
expect localhost:
expect c to retry
frame reconnect-failed
key q
